ix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/Hyperedges-swift.struct/permutations(ofCount:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"permutations(ofCount:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/Hyperedges-swift.struct\/permutations(ofCount:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"permutations","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms20PermutationsSequenceV","text":"PermutationsSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifie